    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-3178",
      "problem": "What is the circumference $C$ of a circle with a diameter of $d=10?$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14183030/assets/b1ebd81fca9688b5688dc916d6be62bad14853f55a8e66c5c7af469dd4032ec4.png)",
      "worked_solution": "We use the formula $C=\\pi d$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\pi d \\\\  & =\\pi \\cdot 10 \\\\  & =10\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the exact answer. If we want an approximate answer, say rounded to three decimal places, we can use the approximation $\\pi\\approx 3.14\\,159,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =10\\cdot \\pi  \\\\  & ≈10\\cdot 3.14\\,159 \\\\  & ≈31.416.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
